1. Signal SparsePostQuantumRatchet — crate `spqr` (post-quantum ratchet / ML-KEM braid)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream:      https://github.com/signalapp/SparsePostQuantumRatchet
Pinned commit: 06959b4708f9b7b1e94d0f8cc835f3958c077e94  (2026-09-16, "Update version to v1.6.0.", crate version 1.6.0)
License:       AGPL-3.0-only (upstream `LICENSE`; crate `Cargo.toml` declares `AGPL-3.0-only`)

How NYX uses it (unmodified):
  * `packages/spqr-wasm/` — a thin Rust wrapper (`src/lib.rs`) that compiles the
    crate to `wasm32-unknown-unknown` (raw module, no `wasm-bindgen`, zero imports).
    `build.sh` generates `Cargo.toml` (not committed, see `.gitignore`) pointing at
    the local pinned checkout via `spqr = { path = "<checkout>/SparsePostQuantumRatchet" }`.
  * Committed build artifact: `packages/spqr-wasm/dist/spqr.wasm` (518,832 bytes).
  * Client use: `web/src/lib/spqrRatchet.ts`, `spqrWire.ts`, `spqrSession.ts`,
    `spqrState.ts`, `spqrNegotiation.ts`, and worker ops
    `spqr_ratchet_init` / `spqr_ratchet_encrypt` / `spqr_ratchet_decrypt`
    (`web/src/workers/crypto.worker.ts`). Design/spec: `docs/33`.

Tests run against the pinned checkout itself (documented in `docs/33` §33.6):
`cargo +nightly test --release --lib` → 57 passed, 0 failed.

