2. Signal libsignal — crate `libsignal-keytrans` (Key Transparency verifier)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream:      https://github.com/signalapp/libsignal
Pinned commit: e8cc2dddd578859b4a029c9c94670b24ce2b616a  (2026-09-22)
License:       AGPL-3.0-only (upstream `LICENSE`; crate declares `license.workspace = true`, workspace license = AGPL-3.0-only)

How NYX uses it (unmodified):
  * `packages/keytrans-wasm/` — thin wrapper (`src/lib.rs`) compiled to
    `wasm32-unknown-unknown` (raw module, no `wasm-bindgen`). `build.sh` generates
    `Cargo.toml` (not committed) with
    `libsignal-keytrans = { path = "<checkout>/rust/keytrans" }`
    (`LIBSIGNAL_PATH`, default `~/signal/libsignal`).
  * Committed build artifact: `packages/keytrans-wasm/dist/keytrans.wasm` (299,846 bytes).
  * Client use: `web/src/lib/keyTransparency.ts` (ops `verify_search`,
    `verify_monitor`, `verify_distinguished`, `monitor_next`, `condense_update`)
    wired into the prekey-bundle trust decision by `ktBundleProof.ts`,
    `ktSubject.ts`, `ktMonitoring.ts`, `peerIdentityTrust.ts`. Design/spec: `docs/34`.

Other parts of libsignal were read only as an implementation reference, without
copying code — e.g. the group sender-key design (`docs/16`). A libsignal-based
cross-implementation ratchet oracle is planned but **not implemented**
(`docs/30` WS-G(6), `docs/11` §11.4).

