3. Signal key-transparency-server (Key Transparency log service, Go)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream:      https://github.com/signalapp/key-transparency-server
Pinned commit: 30b7a2a40604fbe04545d47f26e4c5a35f5d3161  (2026-08-18, "Update go to 1.26.6")
License:       AGPL-3.0-only (upstream `LICENSE`)

How NYX uses it (unmodified upstream packages):
  * `server/kt-query/` — a thin Go service (`main.go`, `query.go`, `write.go`,
    `store.go`, `config.go`) that owns the local LevelDB log and serves NYX's read
    and write paths. The upstream module is **not vendored**: the committed
    `server/kt-query/go.mod` carries

        replace github.com/signalapp/keytransparency => ../../../signal/key-transparency-server

    (upstream module is private and cannot be fetched over the network).
    `server/kt-query/build.sh` re-points that `replace` directive at
    `NYX_KT_UPSTREAM` when the checkout lives elsewhere, and restores it afterwards.
  * Server-side proxy/metrics: `server/src/routes/ktQuery.ts`; client log writer:
    `server/src/utils/keyTransparency.ts` (`docs/32`).

